        "value_sha256": "324143119440754399e2c0a82a4559187d33bc7809dd2c7f4b90ba3e9778d7e7"
      },
      "type": "data_flow",
      "old_value": "Seeds 16 unsigned-byte accumulators with `01 23 45 67 89 AB CD EF FE DC BA 98 76 54 32 10`. For each input index `i` from zero through `len - 1`, it advances `src` and adds that byte modulo 256 to accumulator lane `i % 16`. It then scans lanes 1 through 15, bitwise-inverting a lane when it equals the immediately preceding finalized lane, and copies all 16 resulting bytes to `dest`.",
      "disposition": "retain",
      "reason": "Canonical checksum body and independently read CARDWrite/checksum comparison consumers support the inherited meaning.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "locator": "code://c302741689bd67c361cd7faadb221df3193992c3/src/sysdolphin/baselib/hsd_3B2B.c#L4-L37",
